2026-09-27T07:56:34.1389299Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1389772Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1390486Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1391177Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1391656Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1392181Z ================
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1392479Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1392846Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1393734Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1394276Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1394530Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1395201Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1395633Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1395954Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1396909Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1397818Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1399552Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1400993Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1401247Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1402311Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1403682Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1404390Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1405175Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1406224Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1406778Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1407239Z ========
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1407505Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1410910Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1413606Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1413953Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1414604Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1415712Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1416726Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1417479Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1418085Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1418691Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1418831Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1419158Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1419354Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1420803Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1422370Z 
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1423276Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1424525Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:56:34.1424818Z 
